### Prerequisite: Run orders_http_test.http requests 1 and 2 to set orderId.

### 1. GET existing order item from populated data
GET http://localhost:8081/orderitems/1/426
Accept: application/json

### 2. POST item into newly created order
POST http://localhost:8081/orderitems
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": {{orderId}},
  "productId": 7,
  "quantity": 2,
  "unitPrice": 19.90
}

> {%
  client.test("Item created", function () { client.assert(response.status === 201, "Expected 201"); });
%}

### 3. GET created item
GET http://localhost:8081/orderitems/{{orderId}}/7
Accept: application/json

### 4. GET created order's items
GET http://localhost:8081/orders/{{orderId}}/items
Accept: application/json

### 5. PUT item (stock changes need working SQL UPDATE trigger)
PUT http://localhost:8081/orderitems/{{orderId}}/7
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 5,
  "unitPrice": 17.50
}

### 6. Verify updated item
GET http://localhost:8081/orderitems/{{orderId}}/7
Accept: application/json

### 7. DELETE created item
DELETE http://localhost:8081/orderitems/{{orderId}}/7

### 8. Verify deletion: expected 404
GET http://localhost:8081/orderitems/{{orderId}}/7
Accept: application/json

### 9. Verify order is empty
GET http://localhost:8081/orders/{{orderId}}/items
Accept: application/json

### 10. List only 10 items from large populated database
GET http://localhost:8081/orderitems?page=0&size=10
Accept: application/json

### Follow with orders_http_test.http requests 15 and 16 to delete test order.
